WEBVTT


00:00:20.844 --> 00:00:23.904
<i>Hold on 'cause I'm letting go</i>


00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.516
<i>I'm gonna lasso your heart like a rodeo</i>


00:00:27.684 --> 00:00:31.347
<i>I'm gonna give you some
Till you want some more</i>


00:00:31.521 --> 00:00:35.252
<i>'Cause all I see is an open door</i>


00:00:35.425 --> 00:00:39.225
<i>And I see where it's leading me
All of this energy</i>


00:00:39.395 --> 00:00:42.990
<i>Been bottled up way too long
It's powerful, powerful</i>


00:00:43.166 --> 00:00:46.727
<i>You see what I'm getting at
I'm ready for all of that</i>


00:00:46.903 --> 00:00:50.430
<i>If I'm not a star, you're blind</i>


00:00:50.607 --> 00:00:53.974
<i>I've got rings on my fingers
And glitter in my hair</i>


00:00:54.144 --> 00:00:57.409
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:01.277
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:01.451 --> 00:01:05.478
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:05.655 --> 00:01:09.250
<i>I've got high heel stilettos
And I'm kicking in doors</i>


00:01:09.425 --> 00:01:12.553
<i>And kissing your ass
Ain't what my lipstick's for</i>


00:01:12.729 --> 00:01:16.495
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:16.666 --> 00:01:19.658
<i>I'm gonna run this town
Run this town</i>


00:01:19.836 --> 00:01:23.328
Where's breakfast?
I want waffles, spaghetti!


00:01:23.506 --> 00:01:26.771
Spaghetti waffles! Whoo. Whoo!


00:01:26.943 --> 00:01:28.968
Victor. Victor.
Please wait in the house, please.


00:01:30.413 --> 00:01:33.246
My body is entering hunger shock.


00:01:34.617 --> 00:01:38.314
Oh, bad news.
The cat pooped in the den.


00:01:38.488 --> 00:01:41.787
Worse news, I used your blanket
to clean it up.


00:01:41.958 --> 00:01:43.892
- We don't have a cat.
- No kidding.


00:02:18.995 --> 00:02:22.556
Oh. L... Sorry.
I didn't think you'd be awake.


00:02:22.732 --> 00:02:23.892
You have an appointment...


00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:26.661
...with Guy Morgan,
I didn't think you'd wanna be late.


00:02:26.836 --> 00:02:29.771
Oh, look at you thinking. Cute.


00:02:29.939 --> 00:02:31.998
But I always have time for my portrait.


00:02:32.175 --> 00:02:33.699
Look alive. Paint.


00:02:34.143 --> 00:02:35.974
I'm feeling spiritually blocked.


00:02:36.145 --> 00:02:37.976
Draw me a sesame seed bath.


00:02:38.414 --> 00:02:39.540
Bath. Now.


00:02:40.516 --> 00:02:42.381
Now, make momma look more beautiful
and thinner.


00:02:43.753 --> 00:02:44.981
And make that water more quiet.


00:02:48.558 --> 00:02:50.651
- Bev, you awake?
- Of course I'm awake.


00:02:50.827 --> 00:02:53.421
If I waited for you, I'd never be on time.


00:02:53.596 --> 00:02:56.030
Lucky you never wait for me then.


00:03:09.512 --> 00:03:10.945
Victor, no.


00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:19.554
Uh, don't you want a glass?


00:03:19.722 --> 00:03:25.718
Hmm. Earthy. A tad fishy.
Lovely gravel finish.


00:03:26.195 --> 00:03:28.720
Did you let Victor put worms
in the blender again?


00:03:29.432 --> 00:03:31.127
Yes. I mean, no.


00:03:32.635 --> 00:03:34.227
I mean, it just happened.


00:03:34.771 --> 00:03:36.136
You know nothing can kill me.


00:03:37.307 --> 00:03:38.934
Nothing.


00:03:43.579 --> 00:03:46.446
Step on it, Katie.
I cannot be late for this meeting.


00:03:46.616 --> 00:03:47.981
Just run them over if you have to.


00:03:50.787 --> 00:03:53.813
Hello? No, the kids don't need a library.


00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:57.221
I am the dean, and the dean gets
what she wants, and I wanna remodel.


00:03:57.393 --> 00:04:00.851
You're just boring. I'm being honest.
I don't know what else to tell you.


00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:04.124
And I wanted my office done
for my meeting with Guy Morgan...


00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:05.961
...the music mogul, but no.


00:04:06.135 --> 00:04:08.330
And using Bollywood
as a theme for the dance?


00:04:08.504 --> 00:04:11.962
That's totally un-American.
I don't care if it was my idea.


00:04:13.643 --> 00:04:15.907
Hello.
Oh. Oh.


00:04:16.079 --> 00:04:18.775
I'm Dean Van Ravensway,
and you must be...


00:04:18.948 --> 00:04:22.042
- Guy Morgan.
- Ah, yes. Guy Morgan, a pleasure.


00:04:22.218 --> 00:04:23.708
You look like a man who knows things.


00:04:23.886 --> 00:04:26.446
Aha, even some things I shouldn't know.


00:04:26.622 --> 00:04:28.419
- And I'm Luke.
Great.


00:04:41.971 --> 00:04:45.930
<i>So tell me, Guy, is it true?
Are you the new judge on Idol?</i>


00:04:46.109 --> 00:04:49.476
Well, let's just say
that Randy may be in the doghouse.


00:04:49.645 --> 00:04:51.510
- Now, let's talk about my son.
- Of course.


00:04:51.681 --> 00:04:54.115
- Have you reviewed your schedule, Luke?
- Yes, I have.


00:04:54.283 --> 00:04:57.810
In fact, um, I'd like to add a music class.
Um, the music theory...


00:04:57.987 --> 00:05:01.548
Wellesley has a great business program.
That's why we're here.


00:05:02.058 --> 00:05:06.961
There are two types of people
in the music biz: Artists and businessmen.


00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.961
- Luke is a businessman.
- Of course.


00:05:09.465 --> 00:05:13.458
Katie, get in here. Look alive.
Make yourself useful.


00:05:16.939 --> 00:05:19.271
Luke is gonna need a tour of the campus.


00:05:19.742 --> 00:05:24.805
So text Bev and ask her
to escort Mr. Morgan around campus.


00:05:25.114 --> 00:05:28.242
Now, Luke, if you are half as talented
a producer as your father...


00:05:28.418 --> 00:05:31.478
The verdict's still out.
He hasn't earned it.


00:05:33.156 --> 00:05:35.420
Heard the story of how I started
in the music business?


00:05:35.591 --> 00:05:39.027
- Yes, everybody's heard it, Dad.
- Then everybody should know how it goes.


00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:43.524
There I was,
working for The Rolling Stones...


00:05:43.699 --> 00:05:45.530
...when Mick himself...
- Dad.


00:05:46.803 --> 00:05:50.000
Fine. As I said,
the verdict is still out on my son.


00:05:50.173 --> 00:05:53.939
He just produced an album
with the Fruity Dangers?


00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:55.771
Do you mean Danger Fruit?


00:05:56.946 --> 00:05:58.709
That record was amazing.


00:05:58.881 --> 00:06:01.850
I forgot what they were called because
they made me absolutely no money.


00:06:03.352 --> 00:06:05.820
Thank you. Rare I meet anyone
who's heard their album.


00:06:05.988 --> 00:06:08.889
What, are you kidding?
They're a cult phenomenon.


00:06:09.058 --> 00:06:10.719
I'm sorry. Why are you talking?


00:06:12.261 --> 00:06:17.824
What I need is for Luke to learn
to spot a commercially viable star.


00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.161
Image drives the bottom line, right?


00:06:20.336 --> 00:06:23.703
I feel you. Would we have Bieber Fever
if he were an ugly troll?


00:06:23.873 --> 00:06:26.034
Actually, he is a tad hobbit-like, isn't he?


00:06:26.209 --> 00:06:28.575
I'd like Luke
to produce your Semester Showcase...


00:06:28.744 --> 00:06:32.646
...to see if he can identify sellable talent.
- I produce the Semester Showcase.


00:06:33.783 --> 00:06:35.876
I will double your Showcase budget.


00:06:36.385 --> 00:06:38.751
I will invite every talent scout I know.


00:06:39.322 --> 00:06:41.449
This could be the beginning
of a relationship...


00:06:41.624 --> 00:06:43.592
...between Wellesley
and Kensington Records.


00:06:43.759 --> 00:06:45.750
Looks like we have a new producer.


00:06:45.928 --> 00:06:48.897
Oh, and this is my daughter, Bev.


00:06:49.332 --> 00:06:52.096
Bev, this is the platinum-selling,
Grammy-winning...


00:06:52.268 --> 00:06:55.169
...and very handsome producer,
Guy Morgan.


00:06:55.338 --> 00:06:57.169
Could you give his son, Luke, a tour?


00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:00.207
Sure. Would you like
to see the Wellesley perks?


00:07:00.376 --> 00:07:03.004
Um, yes, brilliant. Sure.


00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.470
- Katie.
I love your accent.


00:07:05.648 --> 00:07:07.240
Katie.
Wanna come over tonight?


00:07:07.416 --> 00:07:09.782
What are you still doing here? Go.


00:07:09.952 --> 00:07:13.353
Guy and I have things we need to discuss.
Out. Now.


00:07:13.956 --> 00:07:19.360
So, Guy, you've gotta tell me,
what was that like working under Mick?


00:07:28.237 --> 00:07:29.932
Watch out.


00:07:30.406 --> 00:07:32.431
- Dangerous balls.
- Ha, ha. Thanks.


00:07:33.442 --> 00:07:37.037
- So you womanned up and did it?
Hey!


00:07:37.213 --> 00:07:39.010
- Oh, I did it.
Hey!


00:07:39.181 --> 00:07:41.547
- What happened?
Can we have our ball?


00:07:41.717 --> 00:07:43.082
I didn't give my CD to Luke.


00:07:43.252 --> 00:07:46.244
I snuck it in his dad's bag.


00:07:46.422 --> 00:07:50.381
But Guy Morgan has your demo.
That's huge. What you need is a champion.


00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.289
No, what I need is to graduate.


00:07:53.129 --> 00:07:55.029
You giving our ball back or what?


00:07:55.197 --> 00:07:58.826
Oh, do you want this?


00:08:03.639 --> 00:08:06.904
She shoots, she scores.
Unlike you, soccer boy.


00:08:09.245 --> 00:08:12.976
Oh, so spill it. Is Luke Morgan
as hot as everyone Tweets he is?


00:08:13.149 --> 00:08:14.514
Hotter.


00:08:14.684 --> 00:08:16.311
You should ask him to the dance.


00:08:16.485 --> 00:08:18.715
Because I'm so forward with guys.


00:08:18.888 --> 00:08:21.448
First time for everything, right?


00:08:28.598 --> 00:08:30.293
- Hi, Luke.
- Hello.


00:08:30.466 --> 00:08:31.694
You have to hear my demo.


00:08:32.168 --> 00:08:35.228
It's a retro-funk-jazz explosion.


00:08:35.404 --> 00:08:37.599
Back off. I was here first.


00:08:37.773 --> 00:08:41.231
Hold on, hold up. Please hold on.
My boy does not want your demos yet.


00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.674
Walk away. Move along. Bye.


00:08:43.846 --> 00:08:47.213
It was nice chatting
or whatever that was.


00:08:47.483 --> 00:08:49.815
- Yes, hi, I'm, uh...
- Luke Morgan, right?


00:08:49.986 --> 00:08:51.510
Who is producing the Showcase.


00:08:51.687 --> 00:08:54.588
I don't think I'm gonna do the Showcase,
so I need to keep a low profile...


00:08:54.757 --> 00:08:58.193
Yeah, yeah. Listen close now.
There's two kinds of people in this school.


00:08:58.361 --> 00:09:01.888
There are the wannabes
and there's gonnabes.


00:09:02.064 --> 00:09:07.229
You and I, we're gonnabes. What do we do?
We stay away from the wannabes, all right?


00:09:07.403 --> 00:09:10.964
And girls named Yolanda. There are three
of them and they are certifiably...


00:09:11.140 --> 00:09:13.233
Crazy? You attract
crazy women? Shocking.


00:09:13.409 --> 00:09:16.310
It may seem like I don't have game,
but ladies love a listener.


00:09:16.479 --> 00:09:18.606
Plus, I'm telling you,
let me help you find acts.


00:09:18.781 --> 00:09:21.807
- Ah, so you're a talent scout?
- Well, bottom line, I'm a DJ.


00:09:21.984 --> 00:09:24.179
- Oh, you're a DJ as well?
- Check this.


00:09:32.728 --> 00:09:33.990
Whoa.


00:09:34.163 --> 00:09:37.257
Okay, yes. You could be very useful.
It was nice meeting you.


00:09:37.433 --> 00:09:40.095
You got a girl for the dance?
Because I can hook you up.


00:09:40.269 --> 00:09:41.429
Uh, no. Thanks.


00:09:41.604 --> 00:09:45.005
Uh, but what do you know
about Bev Van Ravensway?


00:09:45.174 --> 00:09:46.835
- Supposed to see her tonight.
- Bev?


00:09:47.009 --> 00:09:48.033
- Yeah.
- She's hot...


00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:50.678
...but the girl
is mad, mad drama, okay?


00:09:50.846 --> 00:09:53.246
I am talking to you
and you don't even know my name.


00:09:53.416 --> 00:09:55.316
- I'm Mickey O'Malley.
- Mickey O'Malley.


00:09:55.484 --> 00:09:57.111
A rarity in the Irish community.


00:09:57.687 --> 00:09:59.780
Om.


00:10:00.589 --> 00:10:03.217
RAVl: Om.
- Om.


00:10:03.392 --> 00:10:05.485
- Om.
- Om!


00:10:05.661 --> 00:10:08.186
This is not a contest, Ms. Gail.


00:10:08.564 --> 00:10:10.191
Just concentrate on your breathing.


00:10:11.701 --> 00:10:12.861
My butt is numb.


00:10:13.202 --> 00:10:16.399
If your butt is suffering,
then you are suffering.


00:10:16.572 --> 00:10:20.030
In fact, your entire life is suffering. Why?


00:10:20.209 --> 00:10:23.303
Because you crave
that which is meaningless.


00:10:23.479 --> 00:10:25.470
Are you calling me shallow?


00:10:26.549 --> 00:10:32.385
No, I'm saying to stop your craving
and release your butt.


00:10:32.555 --> 00:10:36.116
Just release it. Release it, yeah.
Release that butt.


00:10:36.992 --> 00:10:40.052
<i>Release that butt
Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:40.229 --> 00:10:42.823
<i>Oh, yeah, release that butt</i>


00:10:42.998 --> 00:10:44.295
Mrs. Van Ravensway?


00:10:44.467 --> 00:10:46.992
What part
of "if you interrupt my meditation...


00:10:47.169 --> 00:10:50.366
...I will jerk your tail in a knot"
do you not understand?


00:10:50.539 --> 00:10:52.973
You told me
to tell you when dinner was ready.


00:10:53.142 --> 00:10:56.543
Oh, thank God.
I'm craving some bourbon.


00:11:00.316 --> 00:11:01.783
Victor.


00:11:01.951 --> 00:11:07.184
- Oh. Um, dinner's ready.
- Tell me something I don't know.


00:11:30.846 --> 00:11:35.283
Do you have any idea how stressful it is
to run this academy?


00:11:35.618 --> 00:11:38.109
Yes, I spent the money at the spa.


00:11:39.155 --> 00:11:41.817
<i>Five thousand dollars a night
is not very expensive...</i>


00:11:41.991 --> 00:11:46.553
<i>... when you think about the alternative,
which is me having a nervous breakdown.</i>


00:11:49.865 --> 00:11:50.889
<i>Ow.</i>


00:11:51.066 --> 00:11:53.500
<i>What are you doing?
I'm on the phone.</i>


00:11:53.669 --> 00:11:55.261
<i>- I'm cleansing.
Heh, heh.</i>


00:11:55.471 --> 00:11:57.701
Mac and cheese.


00:11:58.607 --> 00:12:01.735
<i>I don't need your spiritual counseling.</i>


00:12:02.278 --> 00:12:03.836
<i>I'm thinking of firing you.</i>


00:12:09.351 --> 00:12:12.718
Pace yourself, Ms. Gail,
or you will not be one with everything.


00:12:12.888 --> 00:12:16.221
Honey, that's what I got you for.
Now, make me one with everything.


00:12:17.626 --> 00:12:20.823
This Showcase is giving me the vapors.


00:12:20.996 --> 00:12:23.089
How did this become my life?


00:12:23.265 --> 00:12:26.257
Did I ever tell you all about the time
I nearly got my big break?


00:12:26.435 --> 00:12:27.925
Yes.
- Good.


00:12:28.103 --> 00:12:29.536
Then you all know how it goes.


00:12:29.972 --> 00:12:32.167
<i>I ain't gonna leap, I'm gonna jump</i>


00:12:32.341 --> 00:12:34.673
<i>Find my way right out of this dump</i>


00:12:37.513 --> 00:12:40.380
- I had talent, and they made me...
A laughingstock.


00:12:42.151 --> 00:12:43.448
Now look at me.


00:12:43.619 --> 00:12:46.110
I got two ungrateful kids...


00:12:46.288 --> 00:12:49.280
...a dwarfish, hairy, elfin servant...


00:12:49.458 --> 00:12:51.449
...and a random
tablecloth-wearing Asian...


00:12:51.627 --> 00:12:53.857
- Indian.
- Who makes no sense at all, ever.


00:12:54.029 --> 00:12:55.792
Why don't you have another drink, Mom.


00:12:57.333 --> 00:12:59.528
Katie, napkin me.


00:12:59.702 --> 00:13:02.193
I have got to impress Guy Morgan...


00:13:02.605 --> 00:13:05.836
...so I can stop pretending to care
about this insufferable school...


00:13:06.008 --> 00:13:09.774
...and we can all move to Hollywood where
no one pretends to care about anything.


00:13:09.945 --> 00:13:13.574
Mom, I think that you're forgetting
about the most important thing. Me.


00:13:14.516 --> 00:13:16.916
Guy will give me a deal
as soon as he hears me sing.


00:13:17.086 --> 00:13:19.680
- I doubt that.
- No, I've been practicing really hard.


00:13:19.855 --> 00:13:22.722
My voice teacher says
I've transcended to a whole new level.


00:13:22.892 --> 00:13:23.916
Yeah, I doubt it.


00:13:24.093 --> 00:13:26.653
When my first single drops,
I'll buy you that mansion...


00:13:26.829 --> 00:13:28.763
...in the Hollywood Hills...


00:13:28.931 --> 00:13:31.957
...and you can finally afford
to have your legs lengthened.


00:13:32.134 --> 00:13:34.159
- Oh, ba...
- Ms. Gail.


00:13:34.336 --> 00:13:36.304
- Miss Bev has clarity.
Katie.


00:13:36.472 --> 00:13:37.496
- You see...
- Look.


00:13:37.673 --> 00:13:41.541
- The lowly peasant tills the soil
for 40 years without any rain.


00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:45.111
But the unemployed salesman
who has recently discovered hydroponics...


00:13:45.281 --> 00:13:48.375
...all of a sudden gets disgusted by the...
- And see? No sense.


00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:50.848
- That didn't make any sense.
- Let me finish. You...


00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:52.954
Oh, I doubt it. You have me pray all day.


00:13:53.122 --> 00:13:55.352
- I don't feel nothing.
- You don't have a soul.


00:13:55.524 --> 00:13:58.721
No, you don't have soul.
- I have a many souls. I'll give you one.


00:13:58.894 --> 00:14:03.160
- Where's your third eye? Turn that thing on.
- I have a fourth eye too. You wanna see it?


00:14:03.332 --> 00:14:05.300
- What?
- Shh.


00:14:05.801 --> 00:14:09.328
I wanna be 6'4". Wow me, Bev.


00:14:11.874 --> 00:14:17.312
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:17.479 --> 00:14:20.039
Just stop. Stop the wowing, okay?


00:14:20.215 --> 00:14:22.308
What's wrong?
- Somehow you've gotten worse.


00:14:22.484 --> 00:14:24.213
I don't know how that was possible...


00:14:24.386 --> 00:14:27.014
...but there isn't enough Auto-Tune
that's gonna fix you.


00:14:27.189 --> 00:14:30.522
- Well, Katie's bad playing threw me off.
- I don't think it was that.


00:14:30.693 --> 00:14:32.320
Again.


00:14:32.494 --> 00:14:34.052
Really? Okay.


00:14:34.229 --> 00:14:39.861
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do</i>


00:14:40.035 --> 00:14:41.161
Ouch.


00:14:41.337 --> 00:14:44.397
I could belch the song better.


00:14:46.008 --> 00:14:48.169
Have you been drinking
the floor wax again?


00:14:48.344 --> 00:14:49.811
Anything to forget I live here.


00:14:49.979 --> 00:14:52.880
Ugh. My head is buzzing
like a skeeter on a septic tank.


00:14:53.048 --> 00:14:56.950
- Ravi, meditate me.
Good luck, buddy.


00:14:57.319 --> 00:15:00.982
Well, it doesn't matter,
because I have my own plan.


00:15:05.194 --> 00:15:07.560
Does it make me a bad person
that I kind of enjoyed that?


00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:09.459
No.


00:15:09.631 --> 00:15:11.929
Hmm. Nice work.


00:15:24.113 --> 00:15:27.412
- Guess who's on his way over.
- Not now, Victor, I'm busy.


00:15:27.583 --> 00:15:30.051
Guess or prepare to get creamed.


00:15:40.529 --> 00:15:43.623
Victor! Victor! Victor, stop!


00:15:48.504 --> 00:15:50.233
<i>I've got rings on my fingers</i>


00:15:50.406 --> 00:15:51.498
<i>And glitter in my hair</i>


00:15:51.673 --> 00:15:55.769
<i>I've got a one-way ticket
And I just got here</i>


00:15:55.944 --> 00:15:57.275
<i>I'm gonna run...</i>


00:15:57.446 --> 00:16:00.210
- Ha-ha-ha.
- Victor, what are you doing?


00:16:00.649 --> 00:16:01.946
Victor!


00:16:02.117 --> 00:16:05.348
Victor, where did you put my clothes?


00:16:05.521 --> 00:16:07.682
- Surprise!
- What? No.


00:16:11.193 --> 00:16:12.820
I'm gonna kill you. Victor!


00:16:22.738 --> 00:16:23.898
Oh, hi, Katie.


00:16:24.073 --> 00:16:25.472
You are evil. Let me in.


00:16:25.641 --> 00:16:29.077
I control every lock on this property.


00:16:29.244 --> 00:16:30.905
Crap.


00:16:34.316 --> 00:16:36.011
This is insane.


00:16:36.185 --> 00:16:40.246
Yeah, try the shed, it's unlocked, idiot.


00:16:50.032 --> 00:16:52.125
You gotta be kidding me.


00:16:53.869 --> 00:16:55.496
Crap.


00:16:58.807 --> 00:17:02.402
How did such an untalented daughter
spring from my loins?


00:17:02.578 --> 00:17:06.378
Focus, Ms. Gail. We are making
an offering to your personal deity.


00:17:06.548 --> 00:17:08.675
Tell him to give me fame and fortune.


00:17:08.851 --> 00:17:10.546
Not exactly how it works.


00:17:10.719 --> 00:17:13.279
<i>Now, breathe through your Mula Bandha.</i>


00:17:13.455 --> 00:17:16.515
Oh, honey, if I could do that,
I'd get a million hits on YouTube.


00:17:16.692 --> 00:17:18.922
How much longer is this gonna take?
Ugh.


00:17:19.094 --> 00:17:21.221
The prayer or the fame and fortune?


00:17:23.565 --> 00:17:25.032
Ha, ha. See you later.


00:17:31.206 --> 00:17:33.071
Victor.


00:17:36.912 --> 00:17:38.345
Katie?


00:17:39.548 --> 00:17:41.778
- Luke.
- Katie.


00:17:41.984 --> 00:17:45.249
- Are you wearing a doormat?
- Yes.


00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:48.184
- Welcome.
- Why, thank you.


00:17:49.224 --> 00:17:51.055
The truth. Um...


00:17:52.361 --> 00:17:55.694
My stepbrother locked me
outside of the house.


00:17:55.864 --> 00:17:57.195
Naked.


00:17:58.233 --> 00:18:00.531
Oh, sorry. You should...
You should take my jacket.


00:18:00.702 --> 00:18:02.226
Oh.
- Oh, no, no.


00:18:04.673 --> 00:18:05.765
There.


00:18:05.941 --> 00:18:09.138
- Thanks. Now the pants.
- Hmm?


00:18:13.749 --> 00:18:15.376
I'm kidding.


00:18:15.918 --> 00:18:17.749
- You got me.
- Ha, ha.


00:18:18.086 --> 00:18:19.110
No, no.


00:18:19.288 --> 00:18:22.689
One more parent-teacher conference,
I swear I'm gonna lose it.


00:18:22.858 --> 00:18:25.053
Look at me. I'm an educator.


00:18:25.661 --> 00:18:30.325
I have no real skills. And I will die
before I go back to my daddy's farm.


00:18:30.832 --> 00:18:34.632
You tell my personal deity
to help me achieve Guy Morgan. Do it.


00:18:34.803 --> 00:18:37.397
I'll put another banana on the altar.


00:18:41.276 --> 00:18:42.937
What is that?


00:18:43.512 --> 00:18:45.776
Do you hear angels singing?


00:18:45.948 --> 00:18:47.916
Perhaps the gods
have answered your prayer.


00:18:49.117 --> 00:18:50.846
Hey. What...?


00:19:03.699 --> 00:19:06.190
<i>- This is Gail Van Ravensway.
Hello.</i>


00:19:06.368 --> 00:19:07.995
Guy Morgan here. How are you?


00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:10.297
Oh, well, hello, Guy.


00:19:10.472 --> 00:19:12.736
What a surprise
to see you calling this number.


00:19:12.908 --> 00:19:13.932
Do you hear this?


00:19:14.109 --> 00:19:15.770
<i>I can justify</i>


00:19:15.944 --> 00:19:17.639
That's the demo your girl, Katie...


00:19:17.813 --> 00:19:20.145
<i>... slipped into my briefcase.</i>


00:19:20.315 --> 00:19:22.510
And it sounds like money, dear.


00:19:22.684 --> 00:19:24.549
She gave you a CD?


00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:28.087
Oh, well. Well, ain't that the berries.


00:19:29.324 --> 00:19:33.192
Ravi, what frigging god did you pray to?


00:19:34.429 --> 00:19:38.525
Guy, yeah, it seems someone's
not being entirely honest here.


00:19:40.502 --> 00:19:42.697
Katie, somebody get that door!


00:19:43.839 --> 00:19:45.397
So...


00:19:46.275 --> 00:19:48.402
...that meeting today...


00:19:48.577 --> 00:19:51.375
...it was obvious
that your dad doesn't get you.


00:19:51.713 --> 00:19:53.772
He's an idiot for not liking your music.


00:19:53.949 --> 00:19:56.383
Well, it's... It's complicated.


00:19:56.652 --> 00:19:57.846
I'm gonna just, uh...


00:19:59.321 --> 00:20:01.221
Is it as complicated as me...


00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:04.518
...getting stuck outside
in only a welcome mat?


00:20:04.793 --> 00:20:08.524
That's not complicated.
That is a gift from God.


00:20:13.435 --> 00:20:16.233
Luke. Katie. What are you doing?


00:20:16.405 --> 00:20:19.465
Well, it seems your brother
is Satan's very own personal Mini-Me.


00:20:19.641 --> 00:20:21.905
Oh, I know, tell me about it. Come on in.


00:20:25.881 --> 00:20:27.542
Oh, my God, did you work out today?


00:20:29.217 --> 00:20:30.514
- Sit down.
- Ooh, look at this.


00:20:30.686 --> 00:20:33.780
- Ha, ha. Some lemonade.
- Why, thank you.


00:20:33.955 --> 00:20:36.423
You know, my stepsister,
she has body issues...


00:20:36.591 --> 00:20:38.752
...so I don't like
to discourage her nudity.


00:20:38.927 --> 00:20:40.121
That's interesting.


00:20:40.295 --> 00:20:43.059
- She's absolutely lovely...
- Would you like an appetizer?


00:20:43.231 --> 00:20:44.459
<i>Oh, fromage.</i>


00:20:44.633 --> 00:20:46.260
I only have cheese.


00:20:49.438 --> 00:20:51.406
I just got off the phone
with Guy Morgan.


00:20:51.573 --> 00:20:53.473
Your phone.


00:20:56.511 --> 00:20:59.378
He just loved that little demo
you left him.


00:20:59.548 --> 00:21:01.106
I have underestimated you.


00:21:01.683 --> 00:21:03.514
It'd make me proud
if I cared about you.


00:21:03.685 --> 00:21:06.779
- I didn't lie about anything.
- Oh, but, chicken, you did.


00:21:06.955 --> 00:21:09.583
At least that's what Guy thinks,
now that I've clarified.


00:21:09.758 --> 00:21:13.956
I told him it was Bev's demo
and that you stole it from her.


00:21:14.129 --> 00:21:17.394
- But you can't do that. That's my song.
- It's Bev's song.


00:21:17.566 --> 00:21:21.002
And Guy can't wait to see her perform it
at the Showcase.


00:21:21.169 --> 00:21:24.297
If you try to contact him, I'll deny
everything and lock you in the basement.


00:21:24.473 --> 00:21:29.604
- She can't sing to save her life.
- No, but you can, can't you?


00:21:30.879 --> 00:21:33.040
Now, let's hear this amazing voice.


00:21:38.453 --> 00:21:43.083
<i>Like a malignant tumor
She's got no sense of humor</i>


00:21:43.258 --> 00:21:47.354
<i>Just like a swollen blister
It's best to just resist her</i>


00:21:47.529 --> 00:21:51.295
<i>She's not exactly a witch
She's just a terrible bi...</i>


00:21:51.767 --> 00:21:53.428
Well, your lyrics stink.


00:21:53.602 --> 00:21:55.763
But Guy's right, you've got chops.


00:21:59.007 --> 00:22:01.703
Do you know what other instruments
I'm good at?


00:22:02.277 --> 00:22:05.735
I have a feeling I could get in trouble
with a question like that.


00:22:06.181 --> 00:22:08.149
I like trouble.


00:22:09.684 --> 00:22:10.810
Hey, kids.


00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:15.556
- Good evening, Miss Van Ravensway.
- Sorry, I need you to go. Now.


00:22:15.724 --> 00:22:18.488
Family emergency. I need Bev
to help me pass a kidney stone.


00:22:18.660 --> 00:22:22.494
- So she had a lovely evening. Ta-ta.
- Are you trying to ruin my life?


00:22:22.798 --> 00:22:28.031
I have figured out a way for you
to wow Guy Morgan in the Showcase.


00:22:28.236 --> 00:22:30.704
- So you do think I've improved?
- Oh, no, honey.


00:22:30.972 --> 00:22:33.532
But my month of spiritual devotion
has taught me...


00:22:33.708 --> 00:22:35.676
...that God works in annoying ways.


00:22:35.844 --> 00:22:38.904
How am I to wow Guy Morgan
if I supposedly can't sing?


00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:42.140
You can't, but Katie can.


00:22:42.317 --> 00:22:45.013
- What?
- I know. Like I said, annoying.


00:22:45.187 --> 00:22:48.486
We'll record her voice
and you will lip synch.


00:22:48.657 --> 00:22:50.488
What if I don't want to?


00:22:51.593 --> 00:22:55.324
Don't you get snarky with me,
you ungrateful toad.


00:22:55.497 --> 00:22:57.556
- I saved your life.
- You didn't do anything.


00:22:57.732 --> 00:22:59.996
- My dad married you.
- Yeah, and then he died.


00:23:00.168 --> 00:23:03.729
I tried to put you in foster care,
but they was all fulled up on ugly.


00:23:03.905 --> 00:23:05.395
- Funny.
- I thought it was...


00:23:05.574 --> 00:23:07.041
...because you don't wanna look bad.


00:23:08.643 --> 00:23:10.770
Katie, if you don't sing...


00:23:10.946 --> 00:23:14.074
...I'm gonna find a way for that savings
your dad left to disappear.


00:23:14.483 --> 00:23:18.681
That means, you forget college,
moving out, you're stuck here with me.


00:23:18.854 --> 00:23:22.688
But, pumpkin, we're gonna have
so much fun growing old together.


00:23:22.858 --> 00:23:25.759
Why don't you just have her perform
if you like her so much?


00:23:25.927 --> 00:23:28.191
Because, honey, look at you.


00:23:28.363 --> 00:23:30.490
You are a star.


00:23:30.665 --> 00:23:34.863
That is what Guy Morgan needs.
You, the star.


00:23:35.036 --> 00:23:36.594
I'm a star.


00:23:36.771 --> 00:23:40.935
- A bright, gassy star.
- Yes, you are.


00:23:41.109 --> 00:23:43.509
And Guy Morgan is gonna
give you a swimming pool...


00:23:43.678 --> 00:23:45.646
...shaped just like Colin Farrell.


00:23:45.814 --> 00:23:47.372
Every part of him.


00:23:47.549 --> 00:23:51.076
Or, Bev, you could just see every part
of Colin Farrell on the Internet.


00:23:51.253 --> 00:23:54.017
And just leave me out of this.


00:23:55.290 --> 00:23:57.850
- Okay, so how do we do this?
- First rule of Lie Club...


00:23:58.026 --> 00:23:59.926
...is don't talk about Lie Club.


00:24:00.529 --> 00:24:02.429
Which includes you, Katie.


00:24:02.597 --> 00:24:05.293
As far as everyone knows,
you can't sing.


00:24:05.467 --> 00:24:07.526
And no more talking to Luke or Guy.


00:24:07.702 --> 00:24:09.067
Are we clear?


00:24:09.504 --> 00:24:10.698
Crystal.


00:24:12.641 --> 00:24:15.633
Yeah, Dad, we're about to meet
some fresh talent right now.


00:24:15.810 --> 00:24:19.803
Remember when you signed Jay-Z?
No, you passed on him, my bad.


00:24:19.981 --> 00:24:22.449
Um, this is like that,
except it's gonna be brilliant.


00:24:22.617 --> 00:24:23.948
Yeah. Okay.


00:24:24.119 --> 00:24:26.246
- Yeah, okay. Bye.
- Dude, what'd he say?


00:24:26.421 --> 00:24:27.945
These guys you told me about are good?


00:24:28.123 --> 00:24:31.490
Yes. The Oral Majority has potential.
They'll be here any second.


00:24:31.660 --> 00:24:34.356
Talking about potential,
how was your little date with Bev?


00:24:34.529 --> 00:24:36.793
- Her mom kicked me out.
- I told you. Bev is drama.


00:24:36.965 --> 00:24:38.523
Technically, it was Gail's drama.


00:24:38.700 --> 00:24:40.827
But Bev's interesting, man. She's...


00:24:41.002 --> 00:24:42.469
I'm worried she's bonkers.


00:24:42.637 --> 00:24:45.470
See, my last girlfriend, she was hot,
but absolutely mental.


00:24:45.640 --> 00:24:48.302
I need a girl who's not gonna be
shipped to the loony bin.


00:24:48.476 --> 00:24:50.239
Hang on, I'm gonna hit the facilities.


00:24:50.412 --> 00:24:52.107
Facilities. That's a new one.


00:24:52.547 --> 00:24:55.243
- Hey, man. Sorry we're late.
- Hey, what's good, y'all?


00:24:55.417 --> 00:24:58.147
Nobody talks to my boy
until he comes from the facilities.


00:24:58.320 --> 00:24:59.514
We're here to impress.


00:24:59.688 --> 00:25:01.952
- Clear, right?
- Got it.


00:25:05.794 --> 00:25:08.262
<i>When you're fighting just to keep it sane</i>


00:25:08.430 --> 00:25:10.694
<i>Throw your will
At the eye of the hurricane</i>


00:25:10.865 --> 00:25:13.060
<i>- Sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:13.234 --> 00:25:16.601
<i>- Help me sing it out
- Eh-oh, eh-oh, eh-oh</i>


00:25:16.771 --> 00:25:19.296
<i>If you wanna find out who you are
Stop running</i>


00:25:19.474 --> 00:25:22.739
<i>In the end you'll figure out
It's all about nothing</i>


00:25:22.911 --> 00:25:28.213
<i>All night, it's gonna be all right
Hey, hey, hey, hey</i>


00:25:28.383 --> 00:25:35.118
<i>All right
Turn your dreams into your life</i>


00:25:36.324 --> 00:25:37.814
That's good.


00:25:44.866 --> 00:25:48.165
I'm clean. No one followed me.
And I got your intel.


00:25:49.004 --> 00:25:51.336
Oh, Katie, baby, your life sucks.


00:25:51.506 --> 00:25:53.406
Trust me, it gets worse.


00:25:54.442 --> 00:25:58.037
Okay, dude, those guys, they
just went Oral Majority on me in there...


00:25:58.213 --> 00:26:00.408
- I was trying to hold them back...
- You're right.


00:26:00.582 --> 00:26:02.516
They have potential and they're great.


00:26:02.684 --> 00:26:07.917
But first, my talent-finding friend,
promise me no more auditions in the bogs.


00:26:08.089 --> 00:26:10.284
- The what?
- The loo.


00:26:10.825 --> 00:26:12.588
- Bathroom. Toilet.
- Got it.


00:26:12.761 --> 00:26:15.355
All right. Okay, come on.
I wanna show you something.


00:26:15.964 --> 00:26:19.263
So now I have to rehearse in secret.


00:26:19.434 --> 00:26:20.901
Why not not rehearse?


00:26:21.069 --> 00:26:23.094
Make Bev sound bad. What do you care?


00:26:23.271 --> 00:26:26.263
No song, no savings account. No life.


00:26:28.443 --> 00:26:30.877
People. Coming. Now.


00:26:34.416 --> 00:26:36.247
Okay.


00:26:36.818 --> 00:26:39.184
Dude, what are we doing?
The suspense is killing me.


00:26:39.521 --> 00:26:41.284
Can you grab the mike?


00:26:41.456 --> 00:26:43.447
Not about to serenade
a brother, are you?


00:26:43.625 --> 00:26:45.456
Dude, with bromance, comes a fine line.


00:26:45.627 --> 00:26:47.925
That I shall not cross.


00:26:48.396 --> 00:26:50.694
So sing something.


00:26:52.367 --> 00:26:53.834
Okay.


00:26:57.972 --> 00:27:00.770
<i>I'm lost in a world
That rattles my brain</i>


00:27:00.942 --> 00:27:03.433
<i>I'm cleaning up my life
From the mess you made</i>


00:27:03.611 --> 00:27:05.010
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:05.480 --> 00:27:07.471
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:09.284 --> 00:27:11.752
<i>My soul's in debt, but my bills are paid</i>


00:27:11.920 --> 00:27:14.445
<i>I'd give anything just to make an escape</i>


00:27:14.622 --> 00:27:16.214
<i>Oh, oh</i>


00:27:16.725 --> 00:27:18.352
<i>Whoa, oh, oh, oh</i>


00:27:19.360 --> 00:27:22.295
<i>So you can keep
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:22.464 --> 00:27:24.796
<i>Baby, you're rockin'
But there ain't no way I'm ever letting you in</i>


00:27:24.966 --> 00:27:26.433
<i>He's amazing.</i>


00:27:27.836 --> 00:27:29.497
<i>Not again</i>


00:27:30.438 --> 00:27:33.271
<i>So keep on
Knocking, knocking, knocking</i>


00:27:33.441 --> 00:27:38.640
<i>But, baby, you're better off walking
'Cause I ain't gonna let you in</i>


00:27:38.813 --> 00:27:40.371
<i>Never again</i>


00:27:41.483 --> 00:27:44.077
<i>I went out on a limb again</i>


00:27:44.252 --> 00:27:46.812
<i>I guess I had to lose to win</i>


00:27:46.988 --> 00:27:51.357
<i>I was too confused to know
Which way to turn</i>


00:27:52.761 --> 00:27:55.423
<i>- And she could be a millionaire...
- Crap.</i>


00:27:55.597 --> 00:27:57.861
<i>- Gail needs me to drive her home.
- I don't care</i>


00:27:58.032 --> 00:28:00.694
<i>'Cause, baby, there's nobody home</i>


00:28:00.869 --> 00:28:03.360
<i>Nobody's home at all, yeah</i>


00:28:07.842 --> 00:28:09.969
- What? Did you write that?
- Yeah.


00:28:10.145 --> 00:28:12.773
Reminds me of, um... Uh...


00:28:12.947 --> 00:28:16.280
- Danger Fruit, right? Danger Fruit.
- Ha, ha. Because I wrote their album too.


00:28:16.551 --> 00:28:19.042
Shut up. Took me forever
to find that bootleg online.


00:28:19.220 --> 00:28:21.211
- I love that album. That's crazy.
- Yeah.


00:28:21.389 --> 00:28:23.687
My dad doesn't know.
And he thought the record...


00:28:23.858 --> 00:28:25.553
...was a pile of crap.


00:28:25.827 --> 00:28:27.522
He thinks writing's a waste of time.


00:28:27.962 --> 00:28:31.796
Because he basically wants me
to be like him. Only with better hair.


00:28:32.267 --> 00:28:36.363
But the first thing I thought when
I heard those guys in the urinals was...


00:28:36.538 --> 00:28:37.562
...good acoustics.


00:28:37.972 --> 00:28:41.806
Second thought was these guys,
these guys could be great.


00:28:41.976 --> 00:28:43.568
If you gave them your song.


00:28:44.979 --> 00:28:46.640
Mate, that's a brilliant idea.


00:28:47.382 --> 00:28:50.078
- So put them in the Showcase?
- Put them in the Showcase.


00:28:50.251 --> 00:28:51.582
Yeah.


00:28:53.254 --> 00:28:59.784
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:29:00.094 --> 00:29:01.391
You wrote that song today?


00:29:01.563 --> 00:29:05.021
- You've been home for what, two hours?
- It's like an answer to his song.


00:29:05.300 --> 00:29:06.597
You really like this guy.


00:29:06.768 --> 00:29:08.463
Yeah, I'm an idiot.


00:29:08.636 --> 00:29:10.831
You have to sing that for him.


00:29:11.005 --> 00:29:14.497
What if you sang to him in secret?


00:29:16.311 --> 00:29:19.109
At the dance. Ta-da.


00:29:22.717 --> 00:29:25.550
Okay, I know the card's
like, really cheesy, but...


00:29:27.589 --> 00:29:30.057
Oh, God, I hope you like it.


00:29:30.391 --> 00:29:33.883
Ange, it's beautiful,
but are you crazy?


00:29:34.062 --> 00:29:36.087
No, I know you're crazy.


00:29:36.264 --> 00:29:37.288
Am not.


00:29:38.333 --> 00:29:41.325
- What if he doesn't even like me?
- You'll both be in disguise.


00:29:41.502 --> 00:29:44.198
It's your chance to see
if he was really flirting with you.


00:29:44.372 --> 00:29:46.932
I was naked. Of course he was flirting.


00:29:47.108 --> 00:29:49.804
And why even torture myself?
It's not like I can have him.


00:29:49.978 --> 00:29:51.912
Why not? Tell him how you feel.


00:29:52.080 --> 00:29:56.107
If he feels the same way, you can reveal
your hot self and he won't tell Gail.


00:29:56.484 --> 00:29:59.578
And if he hates the song,
leave the disguise on.


00:30:02.523 --> 00:30:04.047
Okay.


00:30:04.359 --> 00:30:05.951
I'm going to the dance.


00:30:06.127 --> 00:30:07.458
That's my girl.


00:30:07.729 --> 00:30:11.722
<i>Maurice, no, no.
Again, in Français, longer legs.</i>


00:30:11.900 --> 00:30:15.199
I wouldn't go in your closet
for a little while if I were you.


00:30:15.370 --> 00:30:17.133
What? Why?


00:30:17.305 --> 00:30:18.670
Hey. Wake up.


00:30:22.577 --> 00:30:24.135
Katie!


00:30:24.312 --> 00:30:27.748
The cat has pooped in my closet.
I need you to clean it up.


00:30:27.916 --> 00:30:29.406
Go.


00:30:29.584 --> 00:30:31.313
I told you we don't have a cat.


00:30:31.486 --> 00:30:32.817
Angie, heads up.


00:30:34.789 --> 00:30:36.086
Katie!


00:30:41.296 --> 00:30:43.025
What's going on?


00:30:43.197 --> 00:30:44.630
Nothing.


00:30:44.799 --> 00:30:47.927
I am, uh, re-organizing and labeling. I...


00:30:48.102 --> 00:30:50.400
I took up crochet.
Do you want new socks?


00:30:50.571 --> 00:30:54.632
I would make you a sweater, but I hear
that the arms, that they're really hard.


00:30:57.879 --> 00:31:02.043
Oh, you thought you could sneak off
and go to the dance.


00:31:02.216 --> 00:31:04.446
After what you pulled today with Guy.


00:31:04.619 --> 00:31:06.052
Oh, no, no.


00:31:06.220 --> 00:31:08.711
Oh, no, no, no.


00:31:08.890 --> 00:31:11.188
You're on Victor watch tonight...


00:31:11.359 --> 00:31:14.055
...tomorrow night and every night.


00:31:14.228 --> 00:31:15.252
Fun.


00:31:15.430 --> 00:31:18.558
I'll give Victor all the mothering
you don't have time for.


00:31:18.733 --> 00:31:22.134
Oh, I wish you could be my mommy.


00:31:23.004 --> 00:31:25.029
I'm off to my cinnamon colonic.


00:31:29.010 --> 00:31:31.376
Hey. Get down.
You're gonna break yourself.


00:31:31.713 --> 00:31:33.977
Or worse, the furniture.


00:31:34.282 --> 00:31:37.376
Hello?
- Hey.


00:31:37.652 --> 00:31:40.815
- You look like you're having fun.
- Always.


00:31:41.155 --> 00:31:44.215
Well, I couldn't let you not go to the dance
without me.


00:31:44.392 --> 00:31:46.792
Besides, we have six hours
of shirtless Team Jacob.


00:31:46.961 --> 00:31:49.896
So let's just get this party started.


00:31:50.064 --> 00:31:54.091
- So is Victor driving you nuts?
- I swear to you, he's not human.


00:31:54.369 --> 00:31:57.668
I mean, can you really blame him, though?
Just look at this family.


00:31:58.873 --> 00:32:00.170
Victor, what are you doing?


00:32:10.151 --> 00:32:12.415
Oh, no. Great.


00:32:12.587 --> 00:32:14.782
Eh, she actually looks prettier
that way.


00:32:15.390 --> 00:32:18.416
True. Ugh. Whatever.


00:32:19.594 --> 00:32:22.722
Why did I ever think that tonight
could've been something special.


00:32:23.498 --> 00:32:25.762
Think Bev's all over Luke at the dance
right now?


00:32:25.933 --> 00:32:28.231
They're probably making out. See?


00:32:28.403 --> 00:32:31.600
- Victor, give it a rest.
- Just check it out. Come on.


00:32:34.809 --> 00:32:37.437
<i>Luke is gonna produce
whoever wins the Showcase.</i>


00:32:37.612 --> 00:32:40.672
<i>So we need a little insurance.</i>


00:32:40.848 --> 00:32:44.045
<i>- I know what I'm doing, Mother.
Do you?</i>


00:32:44.952 --> 00:32:47.819
I can't take it anymore, okay?


00:32:47.989 --> 00:32:50.048
I'm taking my life into my own hands.


00:32:50.224 --> 00:32:51.316
I'm talking to Luke.


00:32:51.926 --> 00:32:54.417
- Finally.
- Okay, but we have gotta be home...


00:32:54.595 --> 00:32:56.062
...before Gail gets here.


00:32:56.798 --> 00:32:58.129
What about the demon spawn?


00:32:58.299 --> 00:32:59.323
Mm-hm.


00:32:59.500 --> 00:33:00.899
Right.


00:33:01.903 --> 00:33:03.302
Okay, just watch him.


00:33:06.374 --> 00:33:07.636
Hmm.


00:33:12.447 --> 00:33:14.438
Is that all you've got, Angela?


00:33:15.116 --> 00:33:16.140
Ravi?


00:33:17.819 --> 00:33:20.344
My sister could catch that, jerknut.


00:33:20.521 --> 00:33:22.955
Put some nuts in that sack, ref.


00:33:25.093 --> 00:33:27.653
Miss Katie, I am most startled.


00:33:27.829 --> 00:33:29.023
Obviously.


00:33:29.564 --> 00:33:32.055
All right. All right. Don't hate me.


00:33:32.233 --> 00:33:33.791
Okay, don't hate me. I'm sorry.


00:33:33.968 --> 00:33:37.335
But my name ain't Ravi. It's Tony.


00:33:37.872 --> 00:33:41.000
- Tony.
- Tony Gupta from Jersey.


00:33:41.175 --> 00:33:43.837
- From Jersey.
- I am half Indian.


00:33:44.212 --> 00:33:47.613
My friends call me Meatball
because I'm half Italian.


00:33:47.782 --> 00:33:49.647
Truth is I always wanted to be an actor.


00:33:50.017 --> 00:33:51.541
But I never got my shot.


00:33:51.719 --> 00:33:53.949
I'm working at KFC,
and one day, Gail comes in...


00:33:54.122 --> 00:33:56.522
...she's like, "Are you Indian?"
I'm like, "What?"


00:33:56.691 --> 00:33:58.886
She's like, "Are you a guru?"
I'm like:


00:33:59.060 --> 00:34:00.550
"Who is asking?"


00:34:00.828 --> 00:34:04.195
She says, "Someone
who's paying for some spiritual guidance."


00:34:04.365 --> 00:34:06.959
And I'm like, "Whaa! It's a miracle!"


00:34:07.135 --> 00:34:11.504
I finally get a chance to do
a total immersion into a character.


00:34:11.806 --> 00:34:14.070
Real training and I get paid.
Are you kidding me?


00:34:14.242 --> 00:34:16.642
Ravi is my King Lear.


00:34:16.978 --> 00:34:19.606
<i>You wanna hear
the monologue from My Fair Lady?</i>


00:34:19.780 --> 00:34:20.974
- Oy, mate.
- No, thanks.


00:34:22.183 --> 00:34:24.879
I'm sorry I barged in. Whoops.


00:34:27.688 --> 00:34:31.351
Your secret's safe with me, okay?
But I need to ask you a favor.


00:34:32.026 --> 00:34:34.085
- Meatball.
- Ha, Meatball.


00:34:34.262 --> 00:34:36.730
Please watch Victor tonight
so I can go to the dance?


00:34:36.898 --> 00:34:37.956
Are you kidding me? Done.


00:34:39.534 --> 00:34:40.865
Blow it up.


00:34:42.803 --> 00:34:44.361
Thank you.


00:34:54.182 --> 00:34:55.581
Whoa.


00:34:55.750 --> 00:34:58.378
How am I supposed to find Luke
if everybody's got a mask?


00:34:58.553 --> 00:35:01.613
I never said this was
gonna be easy. Let's do some recon.


00:35:02.990 --> 00:35:05.322
I am Assistant Principal
Dorothy Plumberg.


00:35:05.493 --> 00:35:08.724
No drinking. No texting. No kissing.


00:35:11.432 --> 00:35:14.401
Luke? No. Luke Morgan?


00:35:14.569 --> 00:35:18.198
No leaving the premises
and no experiencing joy of any kind.


00:35:18.906 --> 00:35:21.238
Luke? Ugh.


00:35:26.614 --> 00:35:28.047
Where is he?


00:35:28.883 --> 00:35:31.681
That reminds me.
I got a new act for you to listen to.


00:35:31.852 --> 00:35:33.513
- Now?
- No time like it.


00:35:33.688 --> 00:35:36.122
- Dude, not again...
- We're called Big Pain Ticket.


00:35:39.627 --> 00:35:43.188
<i>I wanna kiss your apocalypse</i>


00:35:43.364 --> 00:35:46.697
<i>Wrap you in my Armageddon</i>


00:35:46.867 --> 00:35:49.062
<i>Sing you a twisted serenade</i>


00:35:49.270 --> 00:35:52.000
They're good, but I'm worried
that chain saw's unsafe.


00:35:52.173 --> 00:35:54.607
Dude, the chain saw's,
like, the best part.


00:36:01.415 --> 00:36:02.473
I think I found him.


00:36:02.650 --> 00:36:04.914
Well, he is blond.


00:36:08.022 --> 00:36:10.320
Oh, my God, what is she doing here?


00:36:12.226 --> 00:36:14.524
I hate teenage desperation.


00:36:14.695 --> 00:36:16.094
What are you doing here?


00:36:16.264 --> 00:36:19.097
Oh, honey, the prize pig
doesn't win the blue ribbon...


00:36:19.267 --> 00:36:21.292
...by covering up its third best asset.


00:36:21.469 --> 00:36:24.404
A, what does that even mean
and, B, did you just call me a pig?


00:36:24.572 --> 00:36:26.403
Honey, I saw you making sweet love...


00:36:26.574 --> 00:36:29.042
...to a plate of Swedish meatballs
at the snack table.


00:36:31.479 --> 00:36:33.606
It's now or never, babe.


00:36:35.149 --> 00:36:38.585
- What if she recognizes me?
- I'll distract her. Go.


00:36:38.753 --> 00:36:40.948
- So was I right or was I right?
- You were right.


00:36:41.122 --> 00:36:43.989
You have very cool taste.
Any more auditions in the men's...


00:36:44.158 --> 00:36:46.092
...and you're fired.


00:36:49.130 --> 00:36:52.657
- I know your secret.
- Which secret is that?


00:36:55.269 --> 00:36:56.759
I heard you sing at school.


00:36:57.004 --> 00:36:58.130
You were amazing.


00:36:58.306 --> 00:36:59.364
Do I know you?


00:37:03.711 --> 00:37:06.305
- I wanna show you something.
- What's your name?


00:37:08.649 --> 00:37:10.708
Angela, what are you doing?


00:37:11.352 --> 00:37:13.843
I'd like to make a request.


00:37:18.359 --> 00:37:21.192
I will make your night. I promise.


00:37:21.362 --> 00:37:22.727
Miss Van R.


00:37:23.364 --> 00:37:25.764
Is it true you wanted to be a dancer
when you were younger...


00:37:25.933 --> 00:37:27.127
...but were never good enough?


00:37:28.502 --> 00:37:30.163
Who told you that?


00:37:47.888 --> 00:37:49.321
Well, now, how lovely.


00:37:49.490 --> 00:37:52.687
But I've seen better dancing
in a Filipino prison, sugar.


00:37:52.860 --> 00:37:53.986
Oh!


00:37:54.161 --> 00:37:58.393
Really? Because I think
I just challenged you to a dance battle.


00:38:02.737 --> 00:38:05.831
Would Luke Morgan please pick up
the white courtesy phone?


00:38:06.006 --> 00:38:08.907
Luke Morgan, white courtesy phone.


00:38:13.681 --> 00:38:16.411
Hold on. What is that?
You've never seen a guitar before?


00:38:16.751 --> 00:38:19.447
You hid a guitar in there.
You hiding anything else?


00:38:19.620 --> 00:38:20.882
Follow me.


00:38:25.926 --> 00:38:27.757
Oh, wow.


00:38:30.231 --> 00:38:35.794
Madam, while your exquisite eyes
tell of a radiant, but mischievous beauty...


00:38:36.670 --> 00:38:38.570
...I have grown impatient.


00:38:38.739 --> 00:38:42.436
Off with your veil,
so that I may know the truth.


00:38:43.944 --> 00:38:45.138
Or not.


00:38:47.415 --> 00:38:50.441
I'm hoping this answers
a lot of your questions.


00:38:56.657 --> 00:39:00.218
<i>I can see it from the spark in your eyes</i>


00:39:01.529 --> 00:39:05.761
<i>You believe in all the things
You've denied</i>


00:39:05.933 --> 00:39:09.460
<i>You wanna fly
And leave your worries behind</i>


00:39:09.637 --> 00:39:13.630
<i>Don't you? Don't you?</i>


00:39:15.609 --> 00:39:18.942
<i>Well, now I'm knocking
At your front door</i>


00:39:20.714 --> 00:39:24.411
<i>And I'm looking for the right cure</i>


00:39:25.085 --> 00:39:28.782
<i>I'm still a little bit unsure</i>


00:39:29.256 --> 00:39:32.089
Okay, now take off that veil.


00:39:32.560 --> 00:39:33.652
Uh-uh.


00:42:12.586 --> 00:42:15.180
I think I've blown something.


00:42:15.356 --> 00:42:18.416
Does anyone else smell cinnamon?


00:42:21.028 --> 00:42:22.586
Move it, fatso.


00:42:24.331 --> 00:42:30.930
<i>You can never tell where this might go</i>


00:42:31.672 --> 00:42:35.301
Okay, you are blowing my mind.
You have to show me who you are.


00:42:47.855 --> 00:42:49.288
- We have to go.
- What?


00:42:49.456 --> 00:42:51.481
- Come.
- No, Ange.


00:42:51.659 --> 00:42:54.219
In the middle of a really big moment
right now.


00:42:54.395 --> 00:42:56.363
Someone had an accident
and went home.


00:42:58.832 --> 00:43:00.197
I'm so sorry.


00:43:00.901 --> 00:43:02.129
What...? You...?


00:43:02.836 --> 00:43:04.497
Hey. Wait.


00:43:04.672 --> 00:43:05.900
But who are you?


00:43:06.073 --> 00:43:08.667
Over here. Go, go, go.


00:43:16.817 --> 00:43:19.843
- We beat her.
- I love you for this.


00:43:38.305 --> 00:43:40.330
Interesting babysitting attire.


00:43:41.108 --> 00:43:44.043
I should've known
you'd go behind my back again.


00:43:44.478 --> 00:43:47.413
And that Paula Abdul wannabe,
trying to distract me.


00:43:47.748 --> 00:43:49.943
Don't talk about her like that.


00:43:51.952 --> 00:43:55.115
Your friend wants to be a choreographer,
if memory serves.


00:43:55.289 --> 00:43:58.850
She might've made a decent one
if she hadn't gotten herself expelled.


00:43:59.026 --> 00:44:01.290
Guess she can kiss
them Juilliard dreams goodbye.


00:44:01.462 --> 00:44:04.522
Look, I'll do whatever you want.
Okay? Just leave Ange out of this.


00:44:04.832 --> 00:44:07.960
That depends if you pull another stunt
like tonight, sugar.


00:44:08.869 --> 00:44:11.997
- I won't.
- I'll be taking this.


00:44:18.512 --> 00:44:21.743
Only her eyes were piercing out
through this veil, but her voice...


00:44:21.915 --> 00:44:23.974
How hot was the girl
on a scale of one to 10?


00:44:24.151 --> 00:44:26.085
- An 11.
- The hotness scale only goes 10.


00:44:26.253 --> 00:44:27.948
Yeah, this girl has love potential.


00:44:28.122 --> 00:44:30.420
- Ooh, love.
- Shut it.


00:44:31.792 --> 00:44:35.922
We are gonna do this for hours
until we get it right. Even if it takes hours.


00:44:36.897 --> 00:44:40.492
Now, sing like your life depends on it.
Because, sugar, it does.


00:44:41.568 --> 00:44:43.195
We're recording.


00:44:43.504 --> 00:44:45.335
<i>Plug in the mike</i>


00:44:45.506 --> 00:44:46.734
<i>Open the curtain</i>


00:44:47.341 --> 00:44:49.275
<i>Turn on the lights</i>


00:44:49.443 --> 00:44:51.172
<i>I'm through rehearsing</i>


00:44:51.345 --> 00:44:53.677
- Dang, she's good, man.
- Told you, man.


00:44:53.847 --> 00:44:55.075
Check this out, all right?


00:44:55.249 --> 00:44:58.844
Thirty-nine girls in the singing program
which means 85 percent...


00:44:59.019 --> 00:45:00.850
...have music during the sixth period.


00:45:01.021 --> 00:45:02.852
So your girl's in one of those rooms.


00:45:03.056 --> 00:45:05.081
<i>The feeling ignites</i>


00:45:05.259 --> 00:45:06.419
<i>I'm in control</i>


00:45:06.593 --> 00:45:08.561
Oh, cut. Cut.


00:45:08.729 --> 00:45:10.594
That was subpar at best.


00:45:10.764 --> 00:45:13.289
From the top, pretty please.


00:45:14.034 --> 00:45:17.333
<i>Amazing grace</i>


00:45:17.504 --> 00:45:19.062
It's cool, I got this.


00:45:19.239 --> 00:45:21.605
Ladies, all my single ladies.


00:45:21.775 --> 00:45:24.801
My boy Luke here has a special favor
to ask of you, all right?


00:45:24.978 --> 00:45:28.072
He needs vocals
for this big show coming up, so...


00:45:28.248 --> 00:45:29.806
- My name is...
- Luke Morgan.


00:45:30.250 --> 00:45:33.117
You will put me in the Showcase.
Oh, yes, you will.


00:45:33.654 --> 00:45:37.215
- Maybe I could ask you to sing first?
- I am so gonna rock your world.


00:45:37.491 --> 00:45:40.824
<i>I love the way you love me, Luke</i>


00:45:40.994 --> 00:45:43.588
<i>Inside my head every night</i>


00:45:43.764 --> 00:45:46.232
<i>You come and kiss me good night</i>


00:45:46.400 --> 00:45:49.494
<i>Whatever you see is what you get</i>


00:45:49.670 --> 00:45:52.195
Why don't you not suck
and do it again, okay?


00:45:53.941 --> 00:45:58.537
<i>I wanna be with you forever...</i>


00:45:58.712 --> 00:46:01.681
What is going on in here? Disgusting.


00:46:01.849 --> 00:46:04.682
You two boys are not in my class.
Stop. Wait.


00:46:10.724 --> 00:46:13.921
Stop. Wait. Stop.


00:46:33.046 --> 00:46:35.344
<i>I got nothing to lose</i>


00:46:35.515 --> 00:46:36.709
<i>I've been exposed</i>


00:46:36.884 --> 00:46:39.182
<i>I'm paying my dues</i>


00:46:39.353 --> 00:46:40.718
<i>Playing the role</i>


00:46:41.555 --> 00:46:43.682
- Oh, really?
- We are back where we started.


00:46:43.857 --> 00:46:44.983
This is not good.


00:46:46.560 --> 00:46:48.357
That's her. That's her voice.


00:46:48.528 --> 00:46:50.359
Don't think you can get away from me.


00:46:50.530 --> 00:46:52.930
- Step aside. Step aside.
- Please. Wait.


00:46:53.100 --> 00:46:56.536
Okay. But first, why don't you
just both audition for me.


00:46:56.703 --> 00:46:57.727
Listen...


00:46:57.905 --> 00:47:01.341
<i>Luke, you are the one for me, yes you are</i>


00:47:01.508 --> 00:47:03.169
<i>You just don't know it yet</i>


00:47:15.022 --> 00:47:19.015
<i>Make you believe in me</i>


00:47:19.192 --> 00:47:22.184
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:22.362 --> 00:47:25.991
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:26.166 --> 00:47:30.102
<i>That I can be
Anything, anything, anything</i>


00:47:30.270 --> 00:47:34.070
<i>I'll make you believe in me</i>


00:47:34.608 --> 00:47:37.509
<i>I can be what you want me to be</i>


00:47:37.678 --> 00:47:40.738
<i>Tonight is the night
Where I make you see</i>


00:47:42.549 --> 00:47:44.483
It was you?


00:47:45.152 --> 00:47:48.246
- Oh, sorry to interrupt.
- Oh, no, honey. Interrupt away.


00:47:49.189 --> 00:47:53.023
I didn't think I'd see you. It was killing me.
Because I felt like we connected.


00:47:54.661 --> 00:47:57.687
Excuse me.
Uh, how exactly did you two connect?


00:47:57.864 --> 00:48:00.628
Yeah, how did we? I mean, we did.


00:48:00.801 --> 00:48:02.928
- Through...
- With your lyrics. They just...


00:48:03.570 --> 00:48:06.300
- I can't get them out of my head.
- My lyrics. Yeah.


00:48:06.573 --> 00:48:08.336
Well, how wonderful.


00:48:08.508 --> 00:48:11.875
But, uh, Bev has to prepare
for her Showcase audition.


00:48:12.045 --> 00:48:14.309
Oh, no. She doesn't need to audition.
You're in.


00:48:15.816 --> 00:48:17.613
Do you wanna grab a bite later?


00:48:17.784 --> 00:48:18.876
- Yeah.
Wait.


00:48:19.820 --> 00:48:21.287
You have a date with detention.


00:48:21.455 --> 00:48:22.922
Actually, he has a date with me.


00:48:23.090 --> 00:48:24.819
Dear me, did I not fire you?


00:48:24.992 --> 00:48:27.688
- I have tenure.
- One call and you're wearing a paper hat...


00:48:27.861 --> 00:48:30.989
...that says "Welcome to McDonald's.
How may I take your order?"


00:48:31.164 --> 00:48:32.654
- Five calls.
- Two calls and text.


00:48:32.833 --> 00:48:34.733
Two calls, a text, several long e-mails.


00:48:34.901 --> 00:48:37.699
One text and a Tweet.
- One text and a re-Tweet.


00:48:37.871 --> 00:48:40.237
Oh, for God's sakes,
go lick a chalkboard.


00:48:40.407 --> 00:48:41.874
Fine.


00:48:42.676 --> 00:48:44.200
I hate you.


00:48:47.848 --> 00:48:51.978
Okay. Um, I'd love to write a song with you.
Let's talk about it tonight?


00:48:52.252 --> 00:48:54.186
- I'd love to.
- Okay, you're on.


00:49:00.761 --> 00:49:02.388
I've always wanted to write a song.


00:49:02.562 --> 00:49:05.759
Maybe I'll write about my skin.
They say love tightens your pores.


00:49:05.932 --> 00:49:07.399
What rhymes with pores?


00:49:07.567 --> 00:49:10.365
Chores. Bores. Sores.


